  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $p(t)=2{t}^{2}-2t$ onto the subspace spanned by $q(t)=2t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{q(t)}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)=\\frac{\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9}{\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{-1}+(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{0}+(2{t}^{2}\\,-\\,2t){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8+0+0 \\\\  & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2t){|}_{-1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{-1}+(2t){|}_{0}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{0}+(2t){|}_{1}\\,\\cdot \\,(2t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4+0+4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9}{\u27e8q(t),q(t)\u27e9}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{8}\\cdot (2t) \\\\  & =-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
